.TH SSO\-MIB\-LINUX\-ENTRA\-SSO 1 "2026" "@PACKAGE_NAME@ @PACKAGE_VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
linux\-entra\-sso \- native messaging host for the linux-entra-sso webextension
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B linux\-entra\-sso
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B linux\-entra\-sso
reimplements the native messaging host of the
.I linux-entra-sso
webextension on top of the sso-mib library.
.PP
It speaks the WebExtension native messaging protocol on standard input and
standard output, exchanging length-prefixed JSON messages with the browser
extension. Each request is wrapped in a
.RI { command , " message" }
envelope; responses use the same framing.
.PP
The host acquires tokens and cookies from the Microsoft Identity Broker via
DBus and monitors the broker's availability, emitting
.B brokerStateChanged
notifications when the broker appears or vanishes.
.PP
This implementation is intended for experimental purposes, but should be
functionally equivalent to the original host. It can therefore be used as a
drop-in replacement for the native messaging host shipped with the
.I linux-entra-sso
webextension.
.SH COMMANDS
The following commands are accepted in the native messaging
.B command
field:
.TP
.B getAccounts
Return the list of accounts known to the broker.
.TP
.B acquireTokenSilently
Acquire an access token for the account and scopes given in the request. When
no scopes are supplied, the Microsoft Graph default scope is used.
.TP
.B acquirePrtSsoCookie
Acquire a PRT SSO cookie for the requested account, SSO URL and scopes.
.TP
.B getVersion
Return the broker version and the native host version.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B G_MESSAGES_DEBUG=ssomib
Enable debug logging of DBus call parameters via GLib's message logging system.
.SH USAGE
.B linux\-entra\-sso
is not meant to be run interactively. It is launched by the browser through a
native messaging host manifest that points to the installed executable. Refer
to the
.I linux-entra-sso
browser extension documentation for how to register the native messaging host.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The host terminated normally (e.g., standard input was closed).
.TP
.B 1
An error occurred (e.g., the client application could not be created).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sso\-mib\-tool (1)
